---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site handles visits, inquiries, and website drafts.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your information</p>
      <h1 class="serif">Privacy, plainly.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Here’s what happens when you visit, get in touch, or make a website draft.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="prose privacy-copy">
      <h2>Visiting this site</h2>
      <p>This site does not use Google Analytics, advertising pixels, or session replay, and does not set analytics cookies. There is no analytics consent popup.</p>
      <h2>Contacting Drew</h2>
      <p>When you submit the inquiry form, your answers go through Formspree so Drew can receive and respond to your message. The form asks for your name, email address, and message; category and budget are optional. These answers are not sent to analytics. You are not signed up for a mailing list.</p>
      <p>Email and scheduling links open your email app or Calendly. Those services handle the information you provide under their own policies. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy">Calendly’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <h2>Website drafts</h2>
      <p>The experimental website builder reads your résumé and answers in your browser. There is no automatic upload or submission to Drew. The builder and shared-preview pages do not load Google Analytics or session recording.</p>
      <p>A shared preview contains the public fields you approve, encoded in its link. Anyone who has that link can read and forward it. Keep private details out of your approved public text. If you choose to use another AI for help, anything you paste into that AI is handled by that service.</p>
      <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
      <p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Hosting and linked services handle ordinary connection information under their own policies. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>. This site does not use session replay or advertising pixels.</p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Contact <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> with questions about your information.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
